    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Song Dynasty ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> from 960 to 1279, governed by exam-selected scholar-officials rather than generals.</li><li>It ran the world's most commercial economy, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paper-money">paper money</a> and huge cities, and developed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gunpowder">gunpowder</a> weapons, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnetic-compass">compass</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/movable-type">movable type</a>.</li><li>Lacking warhorses and cavalry, it lost the north to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> in 1127 and fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> after four decades of resistance.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bi-sheng">Bi Sheng</a> invented <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/movable-type">movable type</a> using ceramic characters around 1040, some four centuries before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannes-gutenberg">Gutenberg</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> press.</p></aside>
    </section>

